hermes v0.23.0: browser_vault cannot fill a card into hosted card fields
(Stripe Elements, Braintree Hosted Fields, Adyen Secured Fields).

Symptom: on most real checkouts the card number and CVC live in a payment
processor's cross-origin iframe. browser_vault action=fill evaluates only
in the top-level page and answers "No payment form fields were found", and
the browser tool forbids typing a card number, so the agent cannot pay.

Fix (upstream PR as is): with a CDP supervisor, list the iframes the
focused page's own DOM embeds directly (page_child_oopifs), keep those
whose document, read from inside the frame, is on a known processor origin
(PAYMENT_FRAME_ORIGINS) and whose location.ancestorOrigins is exactly
[the item's bound merchant origin]; inspect each with its own nonce, write
the card tokens the frame takes there (never also into the page) with a
fill script bound to the processor origin and wrapped in a re-check of the
ancestry in the same script as the write. Consent, the exact-origin guard
of the merchant page and the backend snapshot run as before.

Plus the test adjustments for running it after
hermes-vault-payment-consent-needs-card.patch (the pre-consent inspection
also counts frame card fields; its tests mock _payment_frames).

Upstream: NousResearch/hermes-agent#136981 (open), commit 26a64bfa1e,
conflict with #126889 resolved. Drop when merged.

